// Title: Processes Accessing the Microphone and Webcam
// Sigma ID: 8cd538a4-62d5-4e83-810b-12d41e428d6e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2020-06-07 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: collection, T1123
// Description: Potential adversaries accessing the microphone and webcam in an endpoint.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/duzvik/status/1269671601852813320
//   - https://medium.com/@7a616368/can-you-track-processes-accessing-the-camera-and-microphone-7e6885b37072
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/builtin/security/win_security_camera_microphone_access.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\CapabilityAccessManager\\ConsentStore\\microphone\\NonPackaged" or RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\CapabilityAccessManager\\ConsentStore\\webcam\\NonPackaged"
